# 08 — ALIASED import with the REAL hint, current behavior (FINDING):
# `import pe "github.com/pkg/errors"` (internal/audit/audit.go) with the
# handoff hint mapping the alias to its real path (["errors","Wrap"]).
# The go provider never applies the 011-02 alias rewrite
# (js_provider does: scope_qualified(...).or_else(scope_qualified_alias
# (...))), so the alias itself is taken as the package name and bails.
# If the provider gains the alias leg, this golden flips to a resolved
# landing into modcache/github.com/pkg/errors@v0.9.1/wrap.go — a
# deliberate diff. NOTE (python-lane P2 lesson): scope carries the REAL
# hint — with an empty scope this probe bails identically and pins
# nothing.
# LAYOUT-BASED: modcache/ is a checked-in directory layout — no go toolchain was run to produce this outcome.
symbol=pe.Wrap
from_file=internal/audit/audit.go
scope=["errors","Wrap"]
root=project
kind=bail
bail=package `pe` is not a required module in go.mod (workspace {root})
